README.OSK -- how this tree differs from Juggle 1.0 as postedORIG/ is the shell archive exactly as Glenn Hutchings posted it toalt.sources on 24 April 1995 (Juggle v1.0): the program, its curses andSilicon Graphics displays, the manual in three forms, and COPYING, the GNUGeneral Public License it is under.  Only the curses display is built;gl.c needs IRIS GL.The program itself is unchanged.  Under -DOSK:  juggle.h     juggle_ball() and juggle_set_step() are declared without               their argument lists: Microware C is K&R and takes no               prototypes.  juggle.c     main(), juggle_set_step() and error() are defined in K&R               form, and M_PI is <math.h>'s PI.  curses.c     juggle_ball() is defined in K&R form.  And juggle_update()               calls unix.l's check_signal() after each frame.  Juggle never               reads the keyboard -- ^C is the only way out, caught by               signal() to put the terminal back -- and that library's               signal() only records the signal; without the call ^C was               noted and ignored and nothing could stop it.  config.h     BSD random() and srandom() are the C library's rand() and               srand().  getopt.c     Henry Spencer's public-domain getopt, which this C library               lacks, as SRC/wump carries it -- with the standard opterr               switch added, because juggle.c clears it to print its own               usage instead of getopt's message.